{
  "$comment": [
    "Slice 6: 1Password product-grouped item regrouping. One item = one",
    "product/subsystem per project; fields = that product's secrets; refs are",
    "op://{Vault}/{Item}/{field}. Environment is encoded in ITEM NAMES:",
    "Postgres items carry an explicit tier (prod/staging/dev); other products",
    "are prod when unsuffixed and staging with a ' staging' suffix. Vault",
    "sensitivity stays exactly where it is today (no ref changes vaults), and",
    "prod-write and prod-RO never share an SA-readable item: RO fields live in",
    "the regular-vault sibling ('Postgres prod RO'). ENVNAMEs never change —",
    "only REFs. pending_source: the OLD item does not exist yet (pending",
    "provisioning/minting/seeding); the new item is minted directly at the",
    "grouped ref later, so copy/verify skip it but apply-refs still rewrites.",
    "LLM keys are per-provider items (OpenAI/Anthropic/Voyage/xAI) for clean",
    "rotation. Field-less prose mentions in docs (e.g. `op://TS/GITHUB_TOKEN`)",
    "are not rewritten by --apply-refs; per-repo PR review catches them.",
    "Consumed by bin/migrate-1p-grouping; old-item deletion is slice 7."
  ],
